      ],
      "source": "https://www.connecticutvisitorguide.com/counties/fairfield/trumbull/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before European settlement, the Golden Hill Paugussett Indian Nation inhabited the area that is now Trumbull Center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.connecticutvisitorguide.com/counties/fairfield/trumbull/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Old Mine Park, part of Trumbull’s 1,400 acres of parks, showcases a fascinating mineral history that attracts geology enthusiasts.",
